  "sourceState": "Scheduling Wave B: the calendar domain engine ported verbatim (all 163 pinned cases green under their pinned names; 159 declarations with two 3-row theories). The pinned packages six executable ambient-clock reads were deliberately not ported - callers supply time and zone ids, deterministic defaults when omitted - and the pinned suite proved the behavior identical. The draft-era local Shipyard.Foundation.Scheduling compatibility copy was replaced at writer-lane merge review with a ProjectReference to the real hlp.foundation.scheduling module to prevent cross-assembly type ambiguity. T-626 promoted the composition to the IAvailabilityRuntime substrate contract (mandatory bounded window, pool capacity by overlap depth, required-resource conjunction with buffers) and routed BookingService through it, removing its duplicate shared-exception resolver.",
